.TH LINUXIO 8 "September 2026" "LinuxIO" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
linuxio \- LinuxIO system administration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxio status
.br
.B linuxio logs
.RI [ component ]
.RI [ lines ]
.br
.B linuxio start
.br
.B linuxio stop
.br
.B linuxio restart
.RB [ \-\-full ]
.br
.B linuxio verbose
.BR enable | disable | status
.br
.B linuxio version
.br
.B linuxio \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxio
is the public command for inspecting and administering the LinuxIO systemd
services.
The other LinuxIO executables are private implementation details installed
under
.IR /usr/libexec/linuxio .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
List the loaded LinuxIO systemd units and their current states.
.TP
.B logs
.RI [ component ]
.RI [ lines ]
Follow LinuxIO messages from the system journal.
.I component
may be
.BR webserver ,
.BR bridge ,
.BR auth ,
or
.BR indexer .
Without a component, messages from all LinuxIO components are shown.
.I lines
is the positive number of existing messages to show before following new
messages; the default is 100.
.TP
.B start
Start
.BR linuxio.target .
.TP
.B stop
Stop
.BR linuxio.target .
.TP
.B restart
.RB [ \-\-full ]
Restart the LinuxIO control plane while leaving the listening webserver socket
active.
With
.BR \-\-full ,
restart the complete
.BR linuxio.target .
.TP
.B verbose
.BR enable | disable | status
Enable, disable, or report verbose logging for the webserver and indexer.
Enabling or disabling verbose logging writes systemd drop-ins, reloads systemd,
and restarts LinuxIO.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed package/build version.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed package/build version.
.SH PRIVILEGES
.B status,
.B version,
and
.B verbose status
do not normally require elevated privileges.
.PP
.B logs
requires permission to read the system journal, normally through root or
membership in the
.B systemd-journal
or
.B adm
group.
The LinuxIO package does not change user group membership.
.PP
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.BR restart ,
.BR "verbose enable" ,
and
.B "verbose disable"
require administrative authorization and are normally run with
.BR sudo (8).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/linuxio/
Administrator-managed LinuxIO configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/linuxio
PAM configuration used for LinuxIO authentication.
.TP
.I /var/lib/linuxio/
Persistent application data.
.TP
.I /run/linuxio/
Runtime sockets and transient status data.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/linuxio/
Private LinuxIO executables managed by the package.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/linuxio*
Package-owned systemd units.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/linuxio-webserver.service.d/verbose.conf
Verbose logging drop-in created by
.BR "linuxio verbose enable" .
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/linuxio-indexer.service.d/verbose.conf
Verbose logging drop-in created by
.BR "linuxio verbose enable" .
.SH SYSTEMD UNITS
.TP
.B linuxio.target
Umbrella target for the LinuxIO application stack.
.TP
.B linuxio-webserver.socket
Listens for browser connections and activates the webserver service.
.TP
.B linuxio-webserver.service
Runs the LinuxIO webserver.
.TP
.B linuxio-auth.socket
Accepts local authentication connections.
.TP
.B linuxio-auth@.service
Runs one authentication worker for each accepted connection.
.TP
.B linuxio-indexer.socket
Activates the filesystem indexer API.
.TP
.B linuxio-indexer.service
Runs the filesystem indexer.
.TP
.B linuxio-indexer-index.timer
Schedules periodic filesystem indexing through
.BR linuxio-indexer-index.service .
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the state of all LinuxIO units:
.PP
.nf
.B linuxio status
.fi
.PP
Follow the latest 200 bridge log messages:
.PP
.nf
.B linuxio logs bridge 200
.fi
.PP
Restart the control plane:
.PP
.nf
.B sudo linuxio restart
.fi
.PP
Restart the complete LinuxIO stack:
.PP
.nf
.B sudo linuxio restart \-\-full
.fi
.PP
Enable verbose logging:
.PP
.nf
.B sudo linuxio verbose enable
.fi
.PP
Print the installed version:
.PP
.nf
.B linuxio \-\-version
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 0 on success and a non-zero status when an
argument is invalid or an operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.socket (5),
.BR systemd.target (5),
.BR sudo (8)
